# Code review

Before calling a feature complete, review correctness, security, performance, scalability, maintainability, tests, error handling, logging, architecture boundaries, database impact, API compatibility, UX, and accessibility.

Flag bugs, vulnerabilities, unnecessary complexity, missing tests, and boundary violations.

Significant changes: Cursor implements → tests → Cursor self-review → Codex (`CODEX.md`) → Claude if architecture/CV/UX is heavy → fixes → tests → human approval. Never approve happy-path-only safety paths.
